Ladybird’s tabs.get(), tabs.remove(), and tabs.reload() fail with
“No tab with id: N.” for a tab the extension can’t see, as Chromium’s
TabsGetFunction, TabsRemoveFunction, and TabsReloadFunction do; and
tabs.remove() closes nothing when any id in its list is unknown. A tab
closes the way the user closing it would, so its page’s beforeunload
handler runs first, which is what Gecko’s ext-tabs.js remove() does
through gBrowser.removeTab() and removeTabs().
